{"id": "unknown-2026-08-22-005", "date": "2026-08-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.33, "keywords": ["growth", "decline", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's trade deficit widens despite 19.6% export rise", "content": "India’s merchandise exports rose 19.6 per cent on-year in July to $44.2 billion, but imports rose 17.5 per cent to $76.2 billion.\nThe goods trade deficit widened to $32.0 billion, keeping cost and currency pressures in focus for sourcing teams.\nReadymade garments, leather, gems and jewellery declined, while growth in cotton yarn, fabrics, and manmade yarn and fabrics moderated.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-trade-deficit-widens-despite-19-6-export-rise-312863-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-22-006", "date": "2026-08-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s road to $20 trn runs through 20 structural reforms: Equirus", "content": "Equirus has proposed a 20-step reform agenda to help India reach a $20 trillion economy by 2036, requiring roughly 18 per cent annual growth in dollar terms. \nThe roadmap focuses on fuel under GST, higher public capex utilisation, deeper capital markets, R&D, education, GCCs, tourism and urban governance. \nEquirus estimates the package could deliver a ₹4.5 trillion annual net fiscal gain. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-road-to-20-trn-runs-through-20-structural-reforms-equirus--312868-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-22-007", "date": "2026-08-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak", "uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Do Bangladesh’s apparel exports to the EU face a tougher road ahead?", "content": "Bangladesh’s apparel exports to the EU fell 16.43 per cent to €8.64 billion in January-June 2026, steepest amongst key suppliers. \nEU apparel imports weakened, but lower unit prices kept Bangladesh’s higher volumes from raising value. \nLDC graduation uncertainty, possible EU-India FTA gains, energy shortages and Chinese and Vietnamese marketing press suppliers on reliability and value addition. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/do-bangladesh-s-apparel-exports-to-the-eu-face-a-tougher-road-ahead--312865-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
